  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFire.BestLeaveBogAgain": "[pg]Perhaps it would be best to leave this faerie fire alone."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFire.BestToLeaveBog": "[pg]Perhaps it would be best to leave this faerie fire alone."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFire.RecallLastEncounter": "You recall your last encounter with one of these 'lanterns' out here in the bog."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFire.SeemsMovingAround": "It seems to be moving around in one of the dense parts of the bog, where the canopy of dead trees and creeping vines create shadows as deep as twilight even at noon.[pg]You can't make out a figure holding the light, but you decide to follow. Spurred on by the thought that it may be someone else like yourself, or perhaps some agent of the demons, you keep trying to catch up with the light up ahead. This trip into the bog is about to pay off."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFire.WadingThroughBog": "As you're wading through the bog a flickering light off in the distance catches your eye. "
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFire.WarningFromTraveler": "[pg]Suddenly a warning from that Traveler's Guide pops into your head. Flickering lights in the swamps and bogs are just swamp gas, it said, unless they're something much worse. Well meaning travelers who follow them are lucky to escape unharmed."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFireLeave.DecideBestNot": "[pg]You decide it's best not to mess with weird floating lights out in the bog and return to your camp."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaFaerieFireLeave.MomentYouDont": "[pg]At the moment you don't feel the need to meet one of those {0} again."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.AboutToAcceptWhen": "[pg]You're about to accept when you notice how a few of the phouka in the back are looking at you. It's a look you recognize from merchants who used to stop in Ingnam to sell their wares. The 'a sucker born every minute' look. You realize none of the phouka have so much as tasted any treacle and you start to wonder what this sugary substance really is."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.AfterMostTake": "[pg]After most of the phouka take another turn pumping the barrels are finally full and one of the goat-morphs hammers a cork into both of them. [say: Ready for that taste o' treacle?] asks the leader, offering you the end of the hose and a small cup."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.BellowsPassedAround": "[pg]The bellows gets passed from phouka to phouka and eventually to your hands. "
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.DontKnowWhy": "You don't know why they said this was difficult. You have no problem pumping the treacle; in fact they have to stop you partway through to change barrels."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.GoatMorphPhouka": "[pg]One of the goat-morph phouka turns to the white cap and says [say: Women aren't supposed to pump treacle.] The white capped phouka growls and turns around, smacking the goat-morph with his cap. [say: I got the cap, I'm the boss round here! I say she can pump, so pump she can!] The boss pulls his cap back on and the goat-morph quickly backs off."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.LookOverSeeTwo": "[pg][say: Hey there! Good timing on yer part. We were just about to stab fer the treacle. Looks like a big load of it, so we'll never get it all in the barrels.] You look over and see two kegs, each about half the size of your water barrels back at camp. Since these phouka seem friendly (and don't seem to want to rape you right now) you decide to take a closer look.[pg]They have excavated a small patch of soil, about 2 feet on a side. Only a foot down there's a seamless black membrane. You've never seen anything like it before, so you ask what they're doing. The phouka with the white cap responds [say: You've never seen treacle mining before? How de you think we get all the sugar?][pg]Since you still look confused he continues. [say: Treacle builds up underground, leaks inta big bubbles like this from tree roots. The bubbles build up a skin of hard black treacle te protect the white treacle.] He gestures at the black substance beneath the soil.[pg]One of the goat-morph phouka stands and comes over. [say: Okay boss, it's all cleaned off.] The phouka you've been talking to buzzes over to the hole and checks it over. [say: Yes, yes. Ye done good work, it's spotless. Is the pump ready?] Another of the goat-morphs nods, holding up a kind of bellows with two hoses sticking out of it. [say: Perfect! Right, two barrels o' treacle comin right up.][pg]He turns back to you and adds [say: Pumping treacle can be exhausting, so if ye give us a hand we'll let you eat some of the leftovers. Unless I missed my guess there's so much down there we'll all be able te eat our fill.]"
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.OnceAgainWading": "Once again you find yourself wading through the cold, wet mire of the bog. You are, as usual, keeping your eyes open for any of the bog's varied inhabitants, but it's your ears that lead you to them. Scraping noises. Loud enough they can't be far off and regular enough that they can't be natural. You ready yourself, your mind imagining all sorts of causes for the noise. No one in this world would bother burying a body, would they? Perhaps a witch is scraping the inside of her cauldron? Wait, why would you even think that? Must be the time of year."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.SneakUpOnSource": "[pg]You sneak up on the source of the sound, a large mound of solid land poking up from the bog, almost like an island. A few twisted trees still cling to life here. What you find is a surprise. In a small clearing are half a dozen phouka. One is buzzing around in faerie form and is wearing a small white cap. The others have taken the form of goat-morphs and are carefully clearing dirt away from something. The one in faerie form spots you and stands up, motioning for you to come over."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.TreaclePumping": "You find that treacle pumping is as hard as the phouka said, but you keep at it. With what you pumped you must be as strong as they are."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.VeryDifficultTo": "You find it very difficult to operate and have to squeeze it with your thighs, but you manage to pump a respectable amount before passing it on."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloween.WhiteHatPullsOut": "[pg]The white hat phouka pulls out a wickedly sharp little knife and uses it to cut a long slit in the black membrane. It sags a little bit and a thick off-white syrup begins to seep through the slit. One of the goat-morphs feeds the tube into the slit and the one with the bellows feeds the other tube into one of the barrels. The phouka begin pumping away and you hear the wet plorping noises of treacle landing in the bottom of the barrel. The clearing is filled with a sugary smell and you start to wonder what treacle tastes like."
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloweenLeave.BetterOffNot": "[pg]Feeling you're better off not finding out you excuse yourself, telling them they can enjoy the treacle amongst themselves. As you walk away you just catch the boss telling the others [say: Watch out fer that one, [He]'s a smart one.]"
  "Scenes.Phoukascene.PhoukaHalloweenTreacleEater.TakeCupAndSqueeze": "You take the cup and squeeze the bellows. Then you tip a bit of the fluid into your mouth and are rewarded with a thick and sweet substance that is also mildly sticky. After rolling it around your mouth you swallow. [say: Well, looks like [he] likes it.] says the boss. You drink a little more. As you do you notice a subtle aftertaste that you have difficulty placing. It's hard to make out through all that sugar.[pg][say: You want some more?] asks the boss. [say: After all, it's always a pleasure to share our treacle with a newcomer.] You try another cup, hoping to work out what that other taste is. You feel like you should be able to place it. After you swallow this batch you notice the grins of the phouka around you. It finally hits you--that other taste is phouka spunk. The phouka see the look on your face and start rolling on the ground laughing.[pg][say: Treacle Mining! And [he] bought it!][pg][say: Oh, ho, 'Pumping treacle can be exhausting'. Oh, boss yer a killer!][pg][say: Boss, you've done it again, yer the master o' the long con, no one can argue that.][pg]Yes, indeed, you've been pranked but good by the little winged bastards. Only a bit of smeared mud hid the fact that the words 'wank tank' were carved into the small barrels. As you storm off towards your camp you hear the leader call out [say: If ye ever want to taste treacle again I've got some for ye. Just ask and I'll put it in yer mouth, instead of yer [if (hasVagina) {cunt|ass}]. Or if you want we can bury it in another barrel and cover it with tarpaper for ya.] Their laughter rings in your ears until after you leave the bog."
